config CPP_FAST_RTTI
	bool "Open hierarchy runtime type information (RTTI) framework"
	help
	  Enable the header-only RTTI framework for C++17 and later. It
	  provides type identification, inheritance checks, and checked
	  pointer casts across class hierarchies, including multiple and
	  virtual inheritance.

	  Classes opt in using RTTI::Enable and RTTI_DECLARE_TYPEINFO.
	  Non-polymorphic types can use RTTI_DECLARE_TRIVIAL to expose
	  compile-time type information without virtual functions.

	  Configure the application for C++17 or a later standard. The
	  compiler-provided RTTI option (CPP_RTTI) can remain disabled.
	  Enabling this option adds the framework's headers to the build.
